targeted by this activity. Lessons and reviews target a topic; diagnostics may target a course, unit, module, or topic. Omit when scope is fully described by the selected content. Course affiliation belongs on activity/course; assignment problem coverage belongs on assigned-problem/topic-coverage. This ordinary ref preserves shared curriculum." :db/id #edb/ref 1049 :db/ident :activity/scope :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 20}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Optional positive finite estimate of the activity's total working time, including adaptive practice. Omit when calculated directly from step estimates." :db/id #edb/ref 1050 :db/ident :activity/expected-seconds :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 57}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Optional positive finite wall-clock limit for the whole activity, measured from the task's first start. Pausing does not extend this limit." :db/id #edb/ref 1051 :db/ident :activity/time-limit-seconds :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 57}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Optional verified Math Academy activity-definition identifier. Captured taskId values belong on learner-task; do not substitute a topic or content ID." :db/id #edb/ref 1052 :db/ident :activity/math-academy-id :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 22}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Stable identity of the activity definition, independent of learner attempts." :db/id #edb/ref 1053 :db/ident :activity/id :db/unique {:db/id #edb/ref 38} :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 56}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Next step in the same activity after a correct answer. Omit when this outcome ends the diagnostic." :db/id #edb/ref 1054 :db/ident :diagnostic-probe/on-correct :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 20}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Next step in the same activity after an incorrect answer when no retry is taken. Omit when this outcome ends the diagnostic." :db/id #edb/ref 1055 :db/ident :diagnostic-probe/on-incorrect :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 20}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Next step in the same activity when the learner explicitly skips the presented question. Omit when this outcome ends the diagnostic. Unpresented questions do not take this branch." :db/id #edb/ref 1056 :db/ident :diagnostic-probe/on-skipped :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 20}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Optional alternate step in the same activity taken when the learner accepts a retry after a submitted incorrect answer. Use a different question on the same topic at the same difficulty, distinguishable from the ordinary incorrect continuation. The completed retry replaces the original result for frontier placement; both presentations remain in history. The application offers the available retry without a timing gate; skips receive no retry. Omit this branch on the alternate step to allow only one retry." :db/id #edb/ref 1057 :db/ident :diagnostic-probe/on-silly-mistake :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 20}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Optional next sibling step under the same activity or multistep owner. The final inner step returns to the enclosing step's continuation. This is presentation order, not a prerequisite edge. Diagnostic steps use outcome branches instead of this linear continuation." :db/id #edb/ref 1058 :db/ident :step/next :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 20}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Optional positive finite expected workload for the whole stage, including any expanded practice. This estimate is not an enforced limit." :db/id #edb/ref 1059 :db/ident :step/expected-seconds :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 57}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Optional positive finite maximum duration for the whole stage, including any expanded practice. Actual learner timing belongs to task records." :db/id #edb/ref 1060 :db/ident :step/time-limit-seconds :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 57}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Optional verified Math Academy step or placement ID. Not a question or content ID." :db/id #edb/ref 1061 :db/ident :step/math-academy-id :db/unique {:db/id #edb/ref 38} :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 22}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Stable identity of a stage in one activity or multistep problem." :db/id #edb/ref 1062 :db/ident :step/id :db/unique {:db/id #edb/ref 38} :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 56}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Tutorial, question (including a worked example), multistep, assigned problem, or knowledge point presented at this stage. An assigned problem references its question or multistep and carries its topic mapping. A multistep expands into its own steps; a knowledge point expands into its canonical example question and adaptive practice. Removing the step preserves its content." :db/id #edb/ref 1063 :db/ident :step/content :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 20}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Complete tutorial body as Markdown with LaTeX, tables, lists, and image links at their intended locations. Document order preserves the sequence of explanation, equations, and illustrations. Tutorials have no fixed problem/solution structure and do not require a gradable response." :db/id #edb/ref 1064 :db/ident :tutorial/content :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 23}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Optional MA tutorial content ID: contentid on a tutorial step in source HTML, or content_id in lesson JSON." :db/id #edb/ref 1065 :db/ident :tutorial/math-academy-id :db/unique {:db/id #edb/ref 38} :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 22}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Stable identity of instructional content, independent of its placement in a lesson." :db/id #edb/ref 1066 :db/ident :tutorial/id :db/unique {:db/id #edb/ref 38} :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 56}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Title of the instructional section, such as Introduction or A Note on Differentiability." :db/id #edb/ref 1067 :db/ident :tutorial/title :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 23}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 36} :db/doc "Owned answer fields. A question may mix radio, blank, select, checkbox, and free fields. Each blank/select has its own key and bank. Each authored checkbox option has its own field, key, two text answers true/false, and one canonical answer. All required fields together form one question; grading produces one question correctness observation. Free fields collect responses and may reveal an optional reference without automatic correctness evidence. Fieldless school prompts remain displayable without grading or mastery credit." :db/id #edb/ref 1068 :db/ident :question/answer-fields :db/isComponent true :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 20}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Optional prefixed Math Academy content identifier: q-N for a source question ID or e-N for a source example content ID. The prefixes prevent overlap in this unique attribute. Identifies content, not a presentation or learner attempt. Omit for independently created content." :db/id #edb/ref 1069 :db/ident :question/math-academy-id :db/unique {:db/id #edb/ref 38} :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 23}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Optional reference to an E/M/H difficulty enum entity observed in completed MA activity: :question.difficulty/easy, /moderate, or /hard. This is distinct from aggregate topic difficulty and learner ability. Omit when unknown; allowed values require validation." :db/id #edb/ref 1070 :db/ident :question/difficulty :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 20}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Problem statement, stored as Markdown supporting LaTeX and image links. For gradable questions, named field locations correspond to answer-field/key on this question's fields. For examples, this is the demonstrated problem." :db/id #edb/ref 1071 :db/ident :question/problem :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 23}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Stable identity of a question or worked example. Individual presentations and submissions have separate identities; changing option order does not create a new question." :db/id #edb/ref 1072 :db/ident :question/id :db/unique {:db/id #edb/ref 38} :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 56}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Whether a calculator is required to answer the question. Captured MA instructions all express a requirement, sometimes specifying a scientific or graphing calculator. This boolean records the requirement only. False means not required, not forbidden; omit when unknown. Absence of a captured instruction alone does not establish false." :db/id #edb/ref 1073 :db/ident :question/requires-calculator :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 24}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Worked solution for the whole problem, stored as Markdown supporting LaTeX and image links. Required for worked examples; optional for ordinary questions." :db/id #edb/ref 1074 :db/ident :question/worked-solution :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 23}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 36} :db/doc "All answer values owned by this field, including authored options, canonical or reference answers, and verbatim learner-entered blank/free responses. Each answer belongs to one field; reuse identical typed values within that field. Radio/select display authored options; blank/free display editors without the bank. Each checkbox option is a separate field owning two text values, true and false. An optional free reference, or the required canonical answer for another type, must belong to this bank. An unanswered free field may have no bank members. Preserve values referenced by task-item/responses." :db/id #edb/ref 1075 :db/ident :answer-field/choices :db/isComponent true :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 20}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Interaction type for this field: :answer-field.type/radio, /checkbox, /blank, /select, or /free. The application checks supported enum membership and type-specific interaction rules. Registering a type does not supply application rendering or evaluation." :db/id #edb/ref 1076 :db/ident :answer-field/type :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 20}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Key unique within the question, binding the field to a problem location such as x or y. A single radio field can use selection without an inline placeholder." :db/id #edb/ref 1077 :db/ident :answer-field/key :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 23}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "One canonical answer, required for radio, select, blank, and checkbox fields; optional reference answer for a free field. When present, it must belong to the field's choices bank. Free references are revealed for comparison without automatic grading. This ordinary ref does not add ownership." :db/id #edb/ref 1078 :db/ident :answer-field/correct :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 20}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Stable identity of a field owned by one question." :db/id #edb/ref 1079 :db/ident :answer-field/id :db/unique {:db/id #edb/ref 38} :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 56}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Exact answer content: learner-entered strings are retained verbatim, including empty or malformed math input. Authored math values may use LaTeX without Markdown delimiters; text and image values hold their respective content. Evaluation and normalization are separate from storage." :db/id #edb/ref 1080 :db/ident :answer/value :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 23}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Optional feedback associated with this answer value, such as an explanation for a radio or select option." :db/id #edb/ref 1081 :db/ident :answer/feedback :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 23}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Representation: answer.type/math, answer.type/text, or answer.type/image." :db/id #edb/ref 1082 :db/ident :answer/type :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 20}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Stable identity of a field-scoped answer value. Reuse this entity for repeated identical values within its field; do not share it across fields." :db/id #edb/ref 1083 :db/ident :answer/id :db/unique {:db/id #edb/ref 38} :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 56}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 36} :db/doc "Immediate generic steps owned by this problem. The collection is unordered; first-step and step/next define presentation order. Do not also add these steps to the enclosing activity's steps." :db/id #edb/ref 1084 :db/ident :multistep/steps :db/isComponent true :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 20}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Optional shared setup, data, diagrams, or instructions in Markdown with LaTeX and image links. Kept available throughout this problem's parts; omit when parts share no setup." :db/id #edb/ref 1085 :db/ident :multistep/context :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 23}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Stable identity of a reusable multipart problem." :db/id #edb/ref 1086 :db/ident :multistep/id :db/unique {:db/id #edb/ref 38} :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 56}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Starting step; must be a member of multistep/steps. This ordinary ref adds no second ownership relationship." :db/id #edb/ref 1087 :db/ident :multistep/first-step :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 20}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 36} :db/doc "Optional mapped topics needed for this problem. The scheduler combines these targets with the enclosing assignment's deadline and learner progress to prioritize preparation. Derive prerequisites from topic/next. Absent coverage means the problem is not yet mapped; coverage does not establish question-bank membership or award mastery." :db/id #edb/ref 1088 :db/ident :assigned-problem/topic-coverage :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 20}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Question or multistep containing the problem itself. This ordinary ref preserves reusable content when the assigned-problem entity is removed." :db/id #edb/ref 1089 :db/ident :assigned-problem/content :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 20}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Stable identity of an externally supplied problem, independent of its placement in an assignment." :db/id #edb/ref 1090 :db/ident :assigned-problem/id :db/unique {:db/id #edb/ref 38} :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 56}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 36} :db/doc "Optional owned question-weight records, defined in 2-question-weights.edn. Each record supplies initial and remedial difficulty distributions for one activity type. Keep at most one record per activity type in this policy; find the policy through the reverse ref. Ensure question-weights/validate on each child. Selection and missing-configuration handling belong to application code." :db/id #edb/ref 1091 :db/ident :policy/question-selection-weights :db/isComponent true :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 20}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Finite upper bound on retention half-life, at least base-half-life-days." :db/id #edb/ref 1092 :db/ident :policy/maximum-half-life-days :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 57}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Finite upper bound on the failure penalty multiplier; at least one." :db/id #edb/ref 1093 :db/ident :policy/maximum-failure-multiplier :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 57}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Finite upper bound on the repetition-credit multiplier; at least one." :db/id #edb/ref 1094 :db/ident :policy/maximum-speed :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 57}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Half-life multiplier per unit of repetition credit. Must be finite and greater than one." :db/id #edb/ref 1095 :db/ident :policy/interval-growth :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 57}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Nonnegative finite exponent controlling the effect of learner accuracy and topic difficulty on repetition credit." :db/id #edb/ref 1096 :db/ident :policy/speed-exponent :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 57}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Nonnegative finite horizon used to compare how much candidate activities postpone upcoming reviews." :db/id #edb/ref 1097 :db/ident :policy/future-horizon-days :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 57}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Nonnegative finite rate at which the failure penalty increases with overdue half-lives." :db/id #edb/ref 1098 :db/ident :policy/overdue-failure-slope :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 57}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Optional explanation of the settings and their intended use." :db/id #edb/ref 1099 :db/ident :policy/description :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 23}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Positive exponent controlling how repetition credit increases as retention falls toward the review threshold." :db/id #edb/ref 1100 :db/ident :policy/early-practice-discount-power :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 57}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Positive lower bound on the repetition-credit multiplier; at most one." :db/id #edb/ref 1101 :db/ident :policy/minimum-speed :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 57}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Retention score assigned on initial learning and reference level used to discount early practice. Positive and finite; later practice can produce a larger score." :db/id #edb/ref 1102 :db/ident :policy/initial-retention :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 57}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Retention score at or below which an established topic is due for review. Positive and below initial-retention; not a recall probability." :db/id #edb/ref 1103 :db/ident :policy/review-threshold :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 57}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Stable identity of this parameter set. Edit its settings under this identity; retained EDB history records previous values. Independent of the engine runtime fingerprint." :db/id #edb/ref 1104 :db/ident :policy/id :db/unique {:db/id #edb/ref 38} :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 56}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Starting accuracy when learner evidence is unavailable; also the default topic difficulty and normalization baseline in the current FIRe model. Strictly between zero and one." :db/id #edb/ref 1105 :db/ident :policy/initial-accuracy :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 57}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Starting retention half-life in days before repetition credit increases it. Must be finite and positive." :db/id #edb/ref 1106 :db/ident :policy/base-half-life-days :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 57}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Supported update order: policy.retention-update/decay-before-add or /add-before-decay. The engine applies the selected ordering explicitly." :db/id #edb/ref 1107 :db/ident :policy/retention-update-order :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 20}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Weight assigned to a new direct answer in the accuracy estimate. Greater than zero and at most one; fractional evidence adjusts this rate in application code." :db/id #edb/ref 1108 :db/ident :policy/accuracy-update-rate :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 57}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Whether positive implicit retention credit is withheld when the topic repetition-credit multiplier is below one." :db/id #edb/ref 1109 :db/ident :policy/gate-slow-implicit :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 24}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Activity-type enum selecting the distribution's use: activity.type/lesson, activity.type/review, or activity.type/assessment. Reuses the enums defined in content/0-activity.edn." :db/id #edb/ref 1110 :db/ident :question-weights/activity-type :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 20}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Relative weight for choosing Easy questions in the initial set. Must be finite and nonnegative; zero excludes this band." :db/id #edb/ref 1111 :db/ident :question-weights/initial-easy :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 57}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Relative weight for choosing Easy questions in the remedial set. Must be finite and nonnegative; zero excludes this band." :db/id #edb/ref 1112 :db/ident :question-weights/remedial-easy :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 57}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Relative weight for choosing Hard questions in the initial set. Must be finite and nonnegative; zero excludes this band." :db/id #edb/ref 1113 :db/ident :question-weights/initial-hard :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 57}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Relative weight for choosing Hard questions in the remedial set. Must be finite and nonnegative; zero excludes this band." :db/id #edb/ref 1114 :db/ident :question-weights/remedial-hard :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 57}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Relative weight for choosing Moderate questions in the initial set. Must be finite and nonnegative; zero excludes this band." :db/id #edb/ref 1115 :db/ident :question-weights/initial-moderate :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 57}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Relative weight for choosing Moderate questions in the remedial set. Must be finite and nonnegative; zero excludes this band." :db/id #edb/ref 1116 :db/ident :question-weights/remedial-moderate :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 57}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 36} :db/doc "Assignments associated with this learner. References activities whose activity/type is activity.type/assignment." :db/id #edb/ref 1117 :db/ident :learner/assignments :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 20}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 36} :db/doc "Longer-term study destinations selected by the learner, displayed with their prerequisite graph. These ordinary refs point to shared topics across courses. Immediate self-directed activities come from learner/queue. Removing a target preserves its topic and all learner history." :db/id #edb/ref 1118 :db/ident :learner/targets :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 20}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 36} :db/doc "Optional collection of learner-specific tasks, including attempts and their history. Each task references a shared activity definition and records its status, elapsed working time, and XP. Status includes completed and failed; there is no separate task outcome. Tasks are defined in 3-learner-task.edn and own the items defined in 3-learner-task.edn. Calendar timestamps and history order come from status transactions. Validate each task and its learner association separately. These ordinary refs do not establish component ownership." :db/id #edb/ref 1119 :db/ident :learner/activity :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 20}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 36} :db/doc "Owned, unordered collection of current progress records, one per topic. Find the learner through the reverse reference learner/_knowledge-profile. Ensure learner/validate when changing membership. Partial imports may contain only known progress facts; ensure progress/validate when writing complete operational state for the engine. Retracting the learner also retracts these records, but not their shared topics." :db/id #edb/ref 1120 :db/ident :learner/knowledge-profile :db/isComponent true :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 20}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 36} :db/doc "Unordered topics explicitly selected by the learner for self-directed study. References shared topics across courses. Adding a topic requests preparation from its existing database lesson content regardless of the selected Study mode. When learner/self-directed is true, Study serves these prepared activities even without engine prerequisite eligibility, without marking them unlocked. Ongoing attempts come first, followed by lower global topic/next layers and then higher scheduling priority within a layer. An empty queue does not fall back to engine recommendations. These ordinary refs do not establish ownership. Removing a queued topic preserves the topic and all learner history. Distinct from learner/targets, which records longer-term study destinations." :db/id #edb/ref 1121 :db/ident :learner/queue :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 20}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Learner-global assessment-only exponentially weighted accuracy in [0,1]. Equal averaging with practice accuracy is described publicly; the precise update rate and prior are local parameters. Update from direct observed answers once, not from every propagated topic update." :db/id #edb/ref 1122 :db/ident :performance/assessment-accuracy :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 57}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Learner-global non-assessment exponentially weighted accuracy in [0,1], kept separate so repeated lesson/review work does not swamp assessment evidence. Update from direct observed answers once, not from every propagated topic update." :db/id #edb/ref 1123 :db/ident :performance/practice-accuracy :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 57}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Learner-global nonnegative effective assessment evidence mass under the local update, distinct from assessment accuracy. Update from direct observed answers once, not from every propagated topic update." :db/id #edb/ref 1124 :db/ident :performance/assessment-mass :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 57}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Learner-global nonnegative effective non-assessment evidence mass under the local update, distinct from practice accuracy. Update from direct observed answers once, not from every propagated topic update." :db/id #edb/ref 1125 :db/ident :performance/practice-mass :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 57}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Optional course currently selected in the UI. References a shared course entity." :db/id #edb/ref 1126 :db/ident :learner/course :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 20}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Optional owned overall performance record, defined in 1-learner.edn. Holds accuracy and evidence mass across topics. Find its learner through learner/_performance; no duplicate learner ref is needed. Ensure performance/validate separately on each performance write. Retracting the learner also retracts this record." :db/id #edb/ref 1127 :db/ident :learner/performance :db/isComponent true :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 20}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Stable learner identity used by the FIRe engine; not a login credential." :db/id #edb/ref 1128 :db/ident :learner/id :db/unique {:db/id #edb/ref 38} :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 23}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "The learner's display name." :db/id #edb/ref 1129 :db/ident :learner/name :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 23}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Whether Study uses the learner's explicitly selected topic queue instead of engine recommendations. Applications should treat an absent value as false." :db/id #edb/ref 1130 :db/ident :learner/self-directed :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 24}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Assessment-only exponentially weighted accuracy in [0,1]. Equal averaging with practice accuracy is described publicly; the precise update rate and prior are local parameters." :db/id #edb/ref 1131 :db/ident :progress/assessment-accuracy :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 57}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Existing topic entity, shared across course contexts." :db/id #edb/ref 1132 :db/ident :progress/topic :db/index true :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 20}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Last direct qualifying practice time, when known; implicit credit does not replace it." :db/id #edb/ref 1133 :db/ident :progress/last-direct-at :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 25}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Non-assessment exponentially weighted accuracy in [0,1], kept separate so repeated lesson/review work does not swamp assessment evidence." :db/id #edb/ref 1134 :db/ident :progress/practice-accuracy :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 57}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Nonnegative effective assessment evidence mass under the local update, distinct from assessment accuracy." :db/id #edb/ref 1135 :db/ident :progress/assessment-mass :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 57}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Nonnegative effective non-assessment evidence mass under the local update." :db/id #edb/ref 1136 :db/ident :progress/practice-mass :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 57}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Nonnegative fractional repetition position. Operational state is clamped at zero; it is not an integer count of reviews." :db/id #edb/ref 1137 :db/ident :progress/repetitions :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 57}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Nonnegative model memory value anchored at memory-at. It is not a probability and need not be at most one." :db/id #edb/ref 1138 :db/ident :progress/memory :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 57}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Optional initial assessment accuracy forecast in [0,1], frozen before the first local outcome. Direct prerequisite assessment accuracies are weighted by their positive assessment masses; fallback is the learner's mass-weighted topic assessment accuracy, then policy/initial-accuracy. This forecast creates no evidence and does not overwrite observed accuracy. Backfilled values are migration-time estimates." :db/id #edb/ref 1139 :db/ident :progress/expected-assessment-accuracy :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 57}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Optional initial practice accuracy forecast in [0,1], frozen before the first local outcome. Direct prerequisite practice accuracies are weighted by their positive practice masses; fallback is the learner's mass-weighted topic practice accuracy, then policy/initial-accuracy. Separate from assessment and from the shared topic workload multiplier. Backfilled values are migration-time estimates." :db/id #edb/ref 1140 :db/ident :progress/expected-practice-accuracy :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 57}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Policy used to compute this state, identified by policy/id. Historical reads at the state-change transaction recover the settings used then; current policy values may have been adjusted since." :db/id #edb/ref 1141 :db/ident :progress/policy :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 20}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Positive finite interval used to decay this anchored memory until the next update. The local interval function determines its value." :db/id #edb/ref 1142 :db/ident :progress/interval-days :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 57}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Stable state identity; update it rather than creating another profile for the same learner-topic pair." :db/id #edb/ref 1143 :db/ident :progress/id :db/unique {:db/id #edb/ref 38} :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 23}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Time at which the stored memory value applies. Compute elapsed days from this anchor once." :db/id #edb/ref 1144 :db/ident :progress/memory-at :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 25}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Whether this topic is admitted to retention tracking after a mastery-learning or explicit initialization decision. True alone does not establish current recall." :db/id #edb/ref 1145 :db/ident :progress/learned :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 24}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 36} :db/doc "Answer entities submitted for this question: entered blank/free values, selected radio/select options, and explicit true or false answers for every checkbox field. Unchecked checkbox options submit false and are not unanswered. Recover each answer's field through reverse answer-field/choices ownership. At most one response per field; identical typed entered values are reused within that field and original strings are preserved. These ordinary refs do not own answers. A free response does not itself assert correct or incorrect." :db/id #edb/ref 1146 :db/ident :task-item/responses :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 20}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 36} :db/doc "Owned question, tutorial, and example presentations, linked in order through task-item/next. The reference collection itself is unordered. Repeated presentations have separate item identities." :db/id #edb/ref 1147 :db/ident :learner-task/items :db/isComponent true :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 20}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Accumulated seconds spent in started, calculated from this item's status transaction history. Paused intervals are excluded. The application updates this value and the parent task's elapsed total together, with at most one actively timed item per learner. Imported observed durations may be retained when their status history is unavailable." :db/id #edb/ref 1148 :db/ident :task-item/elapsed-seconds :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 57}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Accumulated working seconds, calculated by summing task-item/elapsed-seconds across this task's items. The application updates this total with the item durations; it is not an independently edited value or the timed-exam deadline. Omit when durations are unknown." :db/id #edb/ref 1149 :db/ident :learner-task/elapsed-seconds :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 57}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Authored knowledge-point stage deferred after this completed example or answered question because no fresh gradable questions were available. Keeps the practice unfinished while later lesson stages proceed; never a skip, failure, or mastery assertion. Application validates same-activity membership and exhaustion." :db/id #edb/ref 1150 :db/ident :task-item/deferred-step :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 20}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Authored knowledge-point stage revisited by this canonical-example presentation after finishing a lesson route with deferred practice. Replay resumes only outstanding stages and retains prior question outcomes and exposure history. Application validates that the stage was deferred in this task." :db/id #edb/ref 1151 :db/ident :task-item/resumed-step :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 20}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Calculated performance magnitude used by the engine. Positive and finite; may exceed one. Distinct from correctness and XP. Omit until evaluated; the application checks the range." :db/id #edb/ref 1152 :db/ident :task-item/performance :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 57}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Locked means not yet eligible for an engine-selected start; unlocked means engine-eligible but not started. Explicit self-directed queue selections may start a prepared locked task directly without an intermediate unlock. Preparation does not start a clock or establish mastery. Started means in progress; paused means suspended and unfinished, including a lesson route whose completed presentations retain deferred practice markers while waiting for fresh questions. Completed means finished under the activity's completion rules; failed means an explicit task-level failure condition ended the attempt. Status transaction history supplies calendar timestamps, including the first start and terminal transition. Pausing does not extend a timed exam's deadline. Question correctness is recorded by task-item/status; no separate task outcome is stored." :db/id #edb/ref 1153 :db/ident :learner-task/status :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 20}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Numerical scheduling priority; higher values are served first. Eligible unfinished tasks at or above the application's threshold are required. The application calculates finite values and defines the scale and threshold." :db/id #edb/ref 1154 :db/ident :learner-task/priority :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 57}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Optional Math Academy taskId. Reconcile within the learner's history; global uniqueness across learners is not established." :db/id #edb/ref 1155 :db/ident :learner-task/math-academy-id :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 22}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Optional next presentation in the same learner task. Omit on the last item. This ordinary ref orders the task's existing members; learner-task/items remains their component owner. Derive the first item from the member with no incoming next link. The application checks that all members form one chain without cycles, merges, or links outside the task." :db/id #edb/ref 1156 :db/ident :task-item/next :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 20}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Optional nonnegative baseline XP for this attempt, before bonuses or penalties. The displayed denominator is not a maximum." :db/id #edb/ref 1157 :db/ident :learner-task/xp-base :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 22}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Question, worked example question, or tutorial presented. May be absent when historical content identity is unknown." :db/id #edb/ref 1158 :db/ident :task-item/content :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 20}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Shared activity definition for this learner task. Resolve its title, type, and intended scope through this reference." :db/id #edb/ref 1159 :db/ident :learner-task/activity :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 20}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Stable identity of this attempt, independent of external identifiers." :db/id #edb/ref 1160 :db/ident :learner-task/id :db/unique {:db/id #edb/ref 38} :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 56}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Stable identity of this presentation, separate from the content ID." :db/id #edb/ref 1161 :db/ident :task-item/id :db/unique {:db/id #edb/ref 38} :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 56}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Started means actively working; paused suspends the working timer. Completed ends a tutorial, worked example, or submitted question containing free fields whose responses are saved without automatic grading. Correct, incorrect, and skipped end automatically evaluated ordinary question attempts. Retained status history supplies timing. Free response completion does not assert correctness, performance, or mastery credit. Questions never presented do not create task items. Valid transitions and type-specific completion require application validation." :db/id #edb/ref 1162 :db/ident :task-item/status :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 20}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "XP awarded for this attempt, including penalties and bonuses. May be negative or exceed xp-base. Omit when unknown." :db/id #edb/ref 1163 :db/ident :learner-task/xp-earned :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 22}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 36} :db/doc "Optional references from a review or replacement relearning task to the assessment task(s) whose incorrect, skipped, or unanswered-on-expiration topics triggered required practice. One practice task may address obligations from several assessments. The application matches the task topic to each assessment obligation and clears it only after qualifying successful practice; prior or unrelated practice does not count. These links preserve trigger provenance, are not component ownership, and do not themselves enforce scheduling or record invented wrong answers." :db/id #edb/ref 1164 :db/ident :learner-task/remediation-for :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 20}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Optional reference from an assessment retake task to the exact original assessment task. This is an attempt relationship, not activity ownership. The application checks assessment task kinds, prevents self/cyclic links and duplicate generated retakes, selects never-presented questions from the original knowledge points, and offers the retake only after required remediation succeeds. The retake remains optional; this relationship alone does not schedule or require it." :db/id #edb/ref 1165 :db/ident :learner-task/retake-of :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 20}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Latest ordinary queue offer for this task. Records actual inclusion among the five displayed recommendations, rather than preparation alone. Used with finalized review history to derive periodic optional lesson availability; no separate review counter is stored." :db/id #edb/ref 1166 :db/ident :learner-task/offered-at :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 25}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Optional current presentation for freely navigable assessments. References an item owned by this task. Visit order remains in task-item/next; navigation and editable draft responses do not grade a question. The application checks membership and stops edits at whole-assessment submission or expiry." :db/id #edb/ref 1167 :db/ident :learner-task/active-item :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 20}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Repository-relative path to the validated Python generator. Its package records supported templates, difficulty capabilities, finite limits, dependencies and reproducible CLI usage. Registration does not certify arbitrary generated output; generation must pass the content validation and durable commit workflow." :db/id #edb/ref 1168 :db/ident :question-generator/script :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 23}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Stable identity of a validated question generator registered through knowledge-point/question-generator." :db/id #edb/ref 1169 :db/ident :question-generator/id :db/unique {:db/id #edb/ref 38} :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 56}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Optional positive integer daily earned-XP goal across all courses. Days use the learner's local calendar. Absence means no goal has been set. Today and weekly totals are derived from task history, not stored as learner counters." :db/id #edb/ref 1170 :db/ident :learner/daily-xp-goal :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 22}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Optional server-observed submission instant for a terminal question item. Working time ends here, excluding subsequent admission, grading, and database waits even when the status transaction commits later. Absent on older items. Imported duration checkpoints already contain this cutoff when present; dated summaries only count observed started intervals up to this instant." :db/id #edb/ref 1171 :db/ident :task-item/working-ended-at :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 25}}] [{:db/cardinality {:db/id #edb/ref 35} :db/doc "Optional original completion or failure instant recovered from migrated task history. Used for lifecycle ordering, assessment learning age, and dated XP/history instead of the import transaction time. Requires a completed or failed task and must not be later than its recorded terminal status. Omit when the original date is unknown; ordinary task completion uses status transaction history. This does not assert a start or replay learning credit." :db/id #edb/ref 1172 :db/ident :learner-task/finished-at :db/valueType {:db/id #edb/ref 25}}]}
